# Spiral in Livebook

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:spiral_kino, path: Path.join(__DIR__, "..")}
])
```

## Running Spiral

Insert a cell with **+ Smart → Spiral**. The form sets the timeout and whether to show
the generated Rust. The cell compiles with the single-flight Spiral compiler's Rust
backend, `rustc` builds that file, and the program runs. Output, the `i32` value, and
compile errors show up in the cell.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":{"print_code":false,"source":"inl square x = x * x\n\nconsole.write_line \"Hello from Spiral!\"\nsquare 7i32\n","timeout":300},"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl square x = x * x

  console.write_line "Hello from Spiral!"
  square 7i32
  """,
  timeout: 300000
)
```

With **Show generated Rust** the patched Rust is printed before the program output:

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":{"print_code":true,"source":"inl square x = x * x\n\nsquare 7i32\n","timeout":300},"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  inl square x = x * x

  square 7i32
  """,
  timeout: 300000,
  print_code: true
)
```

A body that returns `()` is compiled again with `0i32` so the print still runs. That cell
has output and no value:

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":{"print_code":false,"source":"console.write_line \"Hello from Spiral!\"\n","timeout":300},"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  console.write_line "Hello from Spiral!"
  """,
  timeout: 300000
)
```

`///- --print-code` and `///- --timeout <ms>` on the first `///-` line are honored.
`///> rust` is accepted. Any other `///>` backend raises. A `////` line is dropped.

## Programmatic use

`Spiral.Kino.run/2` returns a `Spiral.Kino.Result`:

```elixir
{:ok, result} = Spiral.Kino.run("1i32 + 2i32", timeout: 120_000)
result.value
```

## Errors

Compile errors are raised as `Spiral.Kino.SpiralError`. Positions refer to the wrapped
`main.spi`:

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":{"print_code":false,"source":"1i32 + \"a\"\n","timeout":300},"chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.Spiral.Kino.SmartCell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Spiral.Kino.eval!(
  ~S"""
  1i32 + "a"
  """,
  timeout: 300000
)
```
